I walk to the next stall.
The stall has many large cheeses.
A friendly vendor smiles at me.
He has a small piece of cheese on a wooden stick.
"Here you go, a small taste," he says.
He gives the stick to me.
I eat the yellow cheese.
It tastes really good.
I look at a small cheese.
"How much does this cheese cost?" I ask.
"It costs fifty-five kroner," the vendor answers.
That is a good price.
I point at the small cheese.
"I will buy it," I say.
He wraps the cheese in paper.
I give him the money.
"Thank you very much," he says.
I put the cheese down into my large bag.
